{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:132aef06340b6938","name":"Womp Rat","source":{"id":"source:reference-132aef06340b6938","title":"Womp Rat","revision":19057,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:13:27Z","sha256":"6d012796981344282b3fec7af67e8271c5cade27b6f012b7db2f4fcb07f92005","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19057","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Womp%20Rat&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-132aef06340b6938","blocks":["\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["Womp Rat Variants\n",{"tag":"p","children":["\n"]},"\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Womp Rat Pack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Womp_Rat_Pack","referenceId":"reference:44798a01dd8461e4"},"\n"],"colspan":2}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"br","children":[]},"\n",{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Womp Rats are large rodents native to the deserts of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},". They breed in sizable colonies and are both scavengers and hunters. Individual Womp Rats subsist by eating carrion or hunting small animals, often including wandering pets and, on rare occasions, small children. Groups of Womp Rats sometimes work together to bring down larger prey, including young ",{"tag":"a","children":["Banthas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Banthas"},", as well as lone ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jawas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jawas"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tusken Raiders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tusken_Raiders"},", or other intelligent beings who find themselves poorly armed and alone. However, they are not especially dangerous except when hunting in groups, and their tactics consist largely of attacking a single target at once.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If there are sufficient numbers of Womp Rats, they are oft willing to attack Medium or Large targets. Although never acclaimed for their bravery, Womp Rats are often renowned for both their endurance and their determination. They are perfectly adapted for life in the deep desert and can go for days without either food or water.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Womp Rat Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Wild Womp Rats are considered vermin by all of Tatooine's sentient ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},". The local government provides a bounty on Womp Rats, and several dozen hermits and eccentrics earn most of their meager living hunting these creatures. Small groups of Womp Rats regularly scavenge garbage on the outskirts of towns, but they rarely come near settlements in large numbers. Although they have never been successfully domesticated, a few people catch young Womp Rats and keep them as half-feral pets. Most often, their owners keep them to guard their homes or businesses, using them as cheaper and less deadly alternatives to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massiffs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massiffs"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Out in the open desert, Womp Rats are far more deadly and regularly travel in packs of up to twenty. On occasion, a large enough pack of Womp Rats have brought down a small ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bantha"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bantha","referenceId":"reference:2948ef2dfab5201a"}," caravan. One of the most dangerous things about Womp Rats is that they are both relatively bright and cowardly. Many learn to recognize a blaster being pointed at them and flee when this happens. Womp Rats almost never attack targets that are Medium or larger without half a dozen or more of their fellows at their side.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Womp Rat Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium Desert ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +7\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 12 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 12, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 11\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 25, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 6 Squares\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," Bite +3 (1d6+2)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"},":"]}," +2, ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Grapple"]